# React TypeScript Frontend Rule

- Use feature-first structure: `features`, `shared`, `components`, `hooks`, `services`, `types`, `schemas`.
- Keep API calls in service/client modules only; UI components should call hooks/query wrappers, not axios/fetch directly.
- Use strongly typed API envelopes and DTOs (`ApiEnvelope`, page result/meta types); avoid `any`.
- Prefer React Query for server state in app modules; keep query keys centralized and stable.
- Validate forms with `zod` schemas and infer form value types from schemas.
- Keep reusable UI in shared packages/components; keep domain-specific UI in app `features`.
- Keep components focused and presentational; move orchestration/business rules into hooks.
- Standardize pagination payloads for backend `/pageable` endpoints (`pageNumber`, `pageSize`, `sortBy`, `sortOrder`, `filter`).
- Normalize API errors in one helper and surface user feedback via shared toast utilities.
- Use path aliases consistently (`@/...`, `@repo/...`, app aliases) and avoid deep relative import chains.
- Default to functional components and typed props; no untyped component exports.

## Example Pattern

```ts
export const useCustomersPage = (body: CustomerPageRequest) =>
  useQuery({
    queryKey: customerKeys.page(JSON.stringify(body)),
    queryFn: () => customerService.page(body),
    placeholderData: keepPreviousData,
  });
```
